      "card_ids": ["C03", "C21", "C25"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Additional cirrhosis-context L1 records show high oral bioavailability for metoclopramide (79 to 82%) and tolfenamic acid (about 91 to 100%), indicating that cirrhosis in this evidence set is associated with high F.",
      "card_ids": ["C06", "C12", "C13", "C23", "C05", "C16"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The closest structural analog azosemide has L1 absolute F of approximately 20.4% in healthy fasted humans, above the threshold; the L2 urinary-recovery estimate of 10% comes from healthy fasted subjects, not cirrhosis, and does not affirm F < 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C04", "C27"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The L3 oral exposure bundle contains no furosemide, bumetanide, or azosemide records; all 50 records concern unrelated molecules and provide no query-specific AUC or Cmax evidence, so they do not alter the level 2 decision.",
