      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C79", "C80", "C49", "C81", "C68", "C84", "C77", "C36", "C38", "C40", "C72", "C45", "C53", "C64", "C42", "C47", "C57", "C69", "C78", "C46"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct furosemide-specific oral bioavailability or exposure record is present in any supplied level.",
    "Azosemide records conflict (L1 20.4% versus L2 10%) and come from healthy fasted subjects, not cirrhosis.",
    "Cirrhosis severity, formulation, and dose effects on furosemide absorption are not specified.",
    "The L3 bundle lacks loop-diuretic exposure records, so it cannot resolve the analog magnitude uncertainty."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because same-class same-condition L1 evidence (bumetanide in cirrhosis, F=95%) and multiple cirrhosis-context records (metoclopramide 79 to 82%, tolfenamic acid about 91 to 100%) support high F; the closest analog azosemide has L1 F=20.4% above threshold. The L3 oral exposure bundle adds no furosemide-specific records and does not change the decision. Confidence remains moderate due to reliance on class transfer and the conflicting azosemide estimates."
}

